# Ford Zodiac Mk I four-door saloon, 1953-1956.
#
# The first Zodiac: the Zephyr Six shell with the larger six, the gold bonnet
# and wing script, and two-tone paint as standard. The Zodiac was two-tone
# only; the three documented combinations share a Dorchester Grey roof and
# upper body, with the lower body in Bristol Fawn, Canterbury Green or
# Winchester Blue.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Zodiac
#
# Dimensions 4.369 x 1.626 x 1.524 m, wheelbase 2.642 m (shared Zephyr shell).
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is a rear
# three-quarter about 50 degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it
# and the other views within the published dimensions. The limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the period Ford dealer leaflet 'Ford Sets The Fashion'
# (1953-54 season), which gives the three Zephyr Zodiac combinations. The
# roof is a fixed Dorchester Grey material and the body is the paint
# material; three colourways, not four. Weights 8, 7, 5, total 20,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 140 km/h. Comfort 58/417, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 58. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1953 intro, retires staggered 1971-1974.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-zodiac-mk1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-zodiac-mk1.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-zodiac-mk1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: image 1 is an oblique rear view, not a scaling elevation,
# so the flank is inherited from the Zephyr Mk I shell. The boot trim is
# simplified, and the two-tone colour boundary is straighter than the
# photographed car's. At 128 px the Dorchester Grey roof, gold script and
# two-tone body read as a Zodiac Mk I.


obj=citycar
